{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow Child Benefit to be backdated to the start of a child\u2019s eligibility",
        "additional_details": "Families shouldn\u2019t lose essential Child Benefit due to lack of awareness, illness, or complex rules. Misleading media reporting about a \u201c2 child cap\u201d caused confusion and delayed claims even where children were legally eligible. It\u2019s unjust that statutory support is paid from the application date, not the true eligibility date.",
        "background": "Amend the Social Security Administration Act 1992 to remove the strict three-month backdating limit for Child Benefit claims.",
